   "set": {
    "popupInfo": {
     "popupElements": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "<p>In the Adams–Onís Treaty of 1819, Spain gave East and West Florida to the United States, and the two countries agreed on a new border between their lands across North America. The United States did not pay Spain for the land. Instead it agreed to pay its own citizens' claims against Spain, up to $5 million.</p>"
      }
     ],
